From fdfbece04061a318c23824c82dffb38877e20265 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:54:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] ntdll: Run WFDXCompat's Rockstar launcher companion on
 Mullion.

WineForge's Rockstar launcher route loads WFDXCompat's D3D11 launcher
companion into Launcher.exe and SocialClubHelper.exe and interposes D3D11
device creation through it. It ran on D3DMetal, which arm64 hosts lack, so
the route was off. Run it on Mullion instead:

- The launcher policy selects Mullion for those processes, and the companion
  when it and Mullion are both present.
- The companion (an ARM64EC build) is found in WFDXCOMPAT_RUNTIME_DIR, by
  default the bundle's lib/wfdxcompat, through a loader alias only those
  processes see.
- When d3d11.dll loads, the companion gets Mullion's D3D11CreateDevice and
  D3D11CreateDeviceAndSwapChain, and GetProcAddress and imports of those and
  of dxgi's DXGID3D10CreateDevice resolve to its wrappers.
- Mullion implements D3D10 devices, context state and GDI surfaces itself, so
  the companion is told to leave them to it (interpose and native D3D10,
  flags 0x9); WFDXCOMPAT_LAUNCHER_FLAGS overrides.
